<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('partials/head') %>
  <title>KAIZEN — Privacy Policy</title>
</head>
<body class="app-page">
  <%- include('partials/navbar') %>
  <main class="app-main" style="max-width:800px;">
    <div class="page-header">
      <div>
        <h1 style="color:var(--gold);">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: June 2026</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px;">
      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:10px;">1. Introduction</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;">
        <p>This Privacy Policy explains how KAIZEN ("we," "us," "our") collects, uses, stores, and protects your information when you use the Platform at kaizen-trader.onrender.com.</p>
        <p>KAIZEN handles sensitive personal information, including your trading behavior and, where you choose to share it, information about your psychological state related to trading. We take this responsibility seriously and aim to be fully transparent about our data practices.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:10px;">2. Information We Collect</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;">
            <h3>Account Information</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Email address</li>
    <li>Username</li>
    <li>Password (stored as a secure hash, never in plain text)</li>
    <li>Google account information, if you register or log in via Google OAuth (name, email, profile ID)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Trading Profile Information</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your stated trading style, including risk per trade, daily drawdown limits, entry and exit rules, trading edge/strategy, emotional triggers, and markets traded</li>
    <li>This information is provided voluntarily during onboarding and can be updated at any time</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Journal Entries</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The free-text descriptions of your trading sessions that you submit</li>
    <li>Whether you indicated rule compliance for each session</li>
    <li>Detected asset, timeframe, and outcome information</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Psychology Session Content</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Messages you send during Psychology Sessions, which may include sensitive information about your emotional state, financial pressures, fears, or mindset related to trading</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Usage Data</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Login times and session activity</li>
    <li>Pages and features accessed within the Platform</li>
    <li>Discipline Score history and streak data</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>On-Chain Data</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>If you connect a Zero Authority DAO account, your ZA user ID and associated reputation data</li>
    <li>A one-way cryptographic hash of your internal user ID may be recorded on the Mantle blockchain, along with discipline score changes, detected patterns, and milestones, all in anonymized form</li>
  </ul>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:10px;">3. How We Use Your Information</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;">
        <p>   We use the information we collect to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Generate AI-powered feedback on your journal entries and psychology sessions</li>
    <li>Calculate and display your Discipline Score</li>
    <li>Detect behavioral patterns across your sessions (such as recurring FOMO or rule violations) to provide more relevant feedback over time</li>
    <li>Send you account-related emails, including welcome emails and, where enabled, weekly summary emails</li>
    <li>Display your position on the community leaderboard, if applicable</li>
    <li>Maintain and improve the Platform</li>
    <li>Investigate and prevent fraud, abuse, or violations of our Terms of Service</li>
  </ul>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:10px;">4. How Your Data Is Processed by Third Parties</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;">
             <p>To provide KAIZEN's core functionality, certain data is shared with third-party service providers:</p>

  <p><strong>Anthropic:</strong> Your journal entries and psychology session messages are sent to Anthropic's Claude API to generate AI feedback. Anthropic processes this text according to their own data handling practices. We do not control how Anthropic's underlying infrastructure processes this data beyond generating the response returned to KAIZEN.</p>

  <p><strong>MongoDB Atlas:</strong> All account data, journal entries, and psychology session content are stored in MongoDB Atlas, a cloud database service. Data is stored in a database we control and is not accessible to MongoDB Atlas employees for any purpose other than infrastructure operation.</p>

  <p><strong>Google:</strong> If you use Google OAuth to register or log in, Google provides us with basic profile information (name, email, profile ID) as authorized by you during the Google sign-in process.</p>

  <p><strong>Resend:</strong> Used to send transactional emails such as welcome messages and weekly summaries. Your email address is shared with Resend solely for this purpose.</p>

  <p><strong>Zero Authority DAO:</strong> If you choose to connect your ZA account, your ZA user ID is used to retrieve your public reputation data from the ZA DAO platform. We do not share your KAIZEN journal content or psychology session content with Zero Authority DAO.</p>

  <p><strong>Mantle Blockchain:</strong> A cryptographic hash of your user ID (not your actual identity, email, or any personal information) is recorded on the Mantle blockchain along with your discipline score changes and detected behavioral patterns, in order to create a verifiable, tamper-proof record of KAIZEN AI's performance. Raw journal text, psychology session content, and any personally identifiable information are never written to any blockchain.</p>

        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:10px;">5. Data Storage and Security</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;">
          <ul>
    <li>Passwords are hashed using bcrypt and are never stored or transmitted in plain text</li>
    <li>Data is transmitted over encrypted HTTPS connections</li>
    <li>Account data is stored in MongoDB Atlas with access restricted to authorized systems</li>
    <li>We implement reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect your data, but no system can be guaranteed 100% secure</li>
  </ul>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:10px;">6. Data Retention</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;">
          <ul>
    <li>Journal entries and AI-generated responses ("Memories") are retained indefinitely to allow KAIZEN to track your behavioral patterns over time and provide increasingly personalized feedback</li>
    <li>If you delete your account, your personal account data, journal entries, and psychology session content will be permanently removed from our active database</li>
    <li>Hashed, anonymized data already recorded on the Mantle blockchain cannot be deleted due to the immutable nature of blockchain technology. However, this data contains no personally identifiable information and cannot be linked back to you without access to our internal database</li>
  </ul>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:10px;">7. Your Rights</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;">
<p>You have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
    <li>Request correction of inaccurate information via your account settings</li>
    <li>Delete your account and associated personal data at any time using the Delete Account feature</li>
    <li>Withdraw consent for non-essential data processing, where applicable</li>
    <li>Request a copy of your data in a portable format by contacting us</li>
  </ul>
    </div>
    <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:10px;">8. Children's Privacy</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;">
           <p>KAIZEN is not intended for individuals under the age of 18. We do not knowingly collect personal information from minors. If we become aware that a user is under 18, we will take steps to delete their account and associated data.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:10px;">9. Cookies and Session Data</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;">
          <p> KAIZEN's infrastructure, including MongoDB Atlas and hosting via Render, may process and store data in regions outside your country of residence. By using KAIZEN, you consent to this transfer and processing of your data.
       </p>
    </div>
    <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:10px;">10. International Data Transfers</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;">
          <p>KAIZEN's infrastructure, including MongoDB Atlas and hosting via Render, may process and store data in regions outside your country of residence. By using KAIZEN, you consent to this transfer and processing of your data.
         </p>
    </div>
    <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:10px;">11. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;">
           <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time as KAIZEN evolves. Material changes will be communicated to users where reasonably possible. Continued use of the Platform after changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the revised Policy.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:10px;">12. Contact Us</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;">
           <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how your data is handled, contact us via X at <strong>@kaizenaibot</strong> or through the Support page on the Platform.
        </p>
    </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
  <script src="/js/app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
